{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1765727,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"blue-dark_un","paid":0,"title":"Bahulya 4.0: A Finance Case Competition \u2013 FIFA World Cup 2030 Edition","festival_id":null,"organization_id":723,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-10-04T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-29T16:30:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/bahulya-40-a-finance-case-competition-fifa-world-cup-2030-edition-jesus-and-mary-college-jmc-du-delhi-1765727","region":"offline","details":"<p>The<strong> Finance and Investment Cell of Jesus and Mary College <\/strong>is proud to present the <strong>fourth edition of Bahulya<\/strong>, a premier finance case competition that challenges participants to showcase their analytical acumen, strategic thinking, and problem-solving skills.<\/p>\n<p>This year&rsquo;s edition explores one of the world&rsquo;s biggest sporting spectacles through a financial lens: the feasibility of hosting the <strong>FIFA World Cup 2030 in India<\/strong>. Participants will be required to navigate the complexities of large-scale infrastructure investment, financing, revenue generation, commercial opportunities, and long-term economic viability.<\/p>\n<p><strong>This Year&rsquo;s Theme: The Feasibility of Hosting the FIFA World Cup in India<br \/><\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>India is evaluating the feasibility of hosting the FIFA World Cup 2030, presenting an ambitious opportunity to combine sporting development with large-scale economic and infrastructural growth.<\/li>\n<li>Participants will assess whether the potential economic and social value generated by the tournament can justify the significant investment required.<\/li>\n<li>The case will require teams to evaluate market demand, revenue potential, capital expenditure, financing structures, host cities, infrastructure, commercial innovation, social impact, risk management, and post-event utilisation.<\/li>\n<li>Teams will be expected to build a financially sound and strategically viable roadmap for hosting the tournament while ensuring that the infrastructure and investments remain sustainable beyond 2030.<\/li>\n<li>No prior knowledge of FIFA is required, only strong financial reasoning, strategic thinking, creativity, and the ability to make data-driven decisions.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>&nbsp;<strong>Guidelines:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Teams of 1&ndash;4 participants.<\/li>\n<li>All rounds are eliminative.<\/li>\n<li>Open to all undergraduate students of the University of Delhi, across colleges, years, and disciplines.<\/li>\n<li>Cross-college and cross-discipline teams are permitted.<\/li>\n<li>Strict no-plagiarism policy applies.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must clearly state their assumptions and justify their financial projections and strategic recommendations.<\/li>\n<li>Adherence to the prescribed submission format and guidelines is mandatory.<\/li>\n<\/ul>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":694378,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-10-04T20:28:13+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-06T19:46:25+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"case_competition","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"zQf1pBe","hashtags":null,"participation_certificate":0,"winner_certificate_at":null,"listed":1,"self_moderated":2,"prizes_release_days":null,"checked":2,"display_title":null,"show_discussions_only_user":1,"show_reviews_only_user":1,"show_score_card":0,"players_count":89,"referral_leaderboard_show":0,"is_ad_free":0,"enable_gamify_leaderboard":0,"tpo_college_id":null,"publish_at":"2026-10-04 23:00:28","auto_shortlist_trigger":false,"enable_ai_discussion":false,"total_unlock_teams":0,"enable_hiring_automation":false,"auto_send_participation_certificate":true,